Done. Tetris is built, working, and fully verified.

What's in place:
- Cargo.toml — ratatui 0.30.2 + crossterm 0.29.0
- src/board.rs — 10x20 grid, collision checks, line clearing
- src/tetromino.rs — all 7 SRS rotation states, spawn positions
- src/rng.rs — small xorshift PRNG + 7-bag shuffle (no deps)
- src/game.rs — gravity, movement, wall-kick rotation, soft/hard drop, scoring, levels, 7-bag randomizer
- src/ui.rs — ratatui rendering: play field, live piece, next preview, score/lines/level panel, control hints
- src/main.rs — terminal setup, raw-mode event loop, game over handling, pause

Verified by actually running it in tmux:
- Field, live piece, next-piece preview, and info panel all render correctly (T piece shown, O next)
- ←/→ moved the piece, ↑ rotated it, space hard-dropped it into the bottom-right, a fresh piece spawned, score updated to 10
- q quit cleanly and the terminal was restored

Quality gates (all green):
- cargo build: zero errors, zero warnings
- cargo clippy --all-targets: zero warnings
- cargo fmt --check: clean
- cargo test: 25/25 pass

Bugs caught and fixed along the way (tests + running it surfaced these):
- clear_lines() was writing survivors to the top instead of dropping them to the bottom — rewrote to fill from the floor up
- drop_interval_ms() would underflow-panic at high levels — switched to saturating arithmetic
- The "next" preview and the field overlay both assumed pieces lived near the origin; a piece at a high column indexed spans out of bounds and panicked mid-game — rewrote the preview to be bounding-box-relative and fixed the overlay index (added a regression test for a wall-hugging piece)
- The 20-row field border was stretching to the terminal's full height; re-anchored it top-aligned with the panel for a proper look

